            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.9 (build 900)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Asobi fills in the where.</b> Source Links opens with what Asobi already knows: where the originals are (grouped by the drive they sit on &#8212; people who mount it open them from there) and every delivery of the package with what it means for a guest. <b>Use What Asobi Knows</b> gives every clip its best source &#8212; a delivery&#8217;s link, else the drive&#8217;s path, else the delivery &#8212; each line says where it came from, links you type are kept as yours.</li>
<li><b>The invite&#8217;s first choice: Let Asobi decide for each person.</b> The invite carries the record; each person&#8217;s copy opens the originals when it mounts the drive, fetches a link when there is one, and otherwise shows where the delivery is and what to do. Under People: which door each person took.</li>
<li><b>&#8220;Your host&#8217;s media&#8221; card</b> on the guest&#8217;s side when the delivery isn&#8217;t a link: where it is, <b>Open Google Drive</b> (or the service), a place to drop the downloaded zip, and &#8212; the moment the zip lands in Downloads &#8212; an <b>Open</b> button for it. Review copies play meanwhile; <b>Tell My Host</b> sends a note.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
